<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75484" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρχ-ηστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>fit for dancing,</i> of the trochaic
			verse, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραμέτρῳ ἐχρῶντο διὰ τὸ σατυρικὴν
					καὶ -ωτέραν εἶναι τὴν ποίησιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1449a23
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. [μέτρον]</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1460a1
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. μέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					583
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					1.21e
				</span></i>
			 ; of persons, <i>good at dancing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.158
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				64
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κὴ τέχνη</span> the <i>art
				of dancing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				816a
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς -κὸν συνεκπίπτοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Longin.
					41.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>pantomimic,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Salt.</u>
				31
			</span></i>.—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρχηστρικός</span> is
			perh. 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρχηστικός</span>
			 in Theopomp.Hist.III(<i>a</i>).</div>
